    22	/**
    23	 * Wrap a Cloudflare Worker RPC stub in a `Promise<T>`-shaped proxy so callers
    24	 * outside the Effect runtime (TanStack Start route handlers, plain Workers,
    25	 * test code) can `await` RPC methods directly.
    26	 *
    27	 * The proxy:
    28	 * - leaves `fetch` / `connect` / `Symbol.dispose` and other non-string keys
    29	 *   passing through to the underlying binding unchanged,
    30	 * - turns each `Effect<T>` / `Stream<T>` method into a `Promise<T>` /
    31	 *   `Promise<ReadableStream<Uint8Array>>`,
    32	 * - unwraps the wire envelopes produced by the Effect-side RPC bridge:
    33	 *   `RpcErrorEnvelope` is rethrown via {@link decodeRpcThrowable} so
    34	 *   `try/catch` sees an `Error` (or a tagged error object), and
    35	 *   `RpcStreamEnvelope` is flattened to its `ReadableStream` body.
    36	 *
    37	 * @example Three ways to reach a value from a plain Worker — direct binding, fetch, RPC
    38	 * ```ts
    39	 * import { toRpcAsync } from "alchemy/Cloudflare/Bridge";
    40	 * import type Backend from "./backend.ts";
    41	 *
    42	 * interface Env {
    43	 *   BUCKET: Bucket;
    44	 *   BACKEND: Service<Backend>;
    45	 * }
